---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

import Hero from '~/components/widgets/Hero.astro';
import Content from '~/components/widgets/Content.astro';
import Features from '~/components/widgets/Features.astro';
import CallToAction from '~/components/widgets/CallToAction.astro';
import { getPermalink } from '~/utils/permalinks';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Mia Consultancy: Bridging Potential with Purpose',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- Hero Widget ******************* -->

  <Hero
    tagline="Mia Consultancy"
    actions={[
      { variant: 'primary', text: 'Explore our core competencies', href: getPermalink('/expertise') },
      { text: 'Talk to us', href: getPermalink('/contact') },
    ]}
    image={{
      src: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552664730-d307ca884978?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=1740&q=80',
      alt: 'Consulting team collaborating in a meeting room',
    }}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">Bridging potential with purpose.</Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      From elite sport to organizations, we design evidence-based psychological and organisational solutions that
      empower young professionals and strengthen the organisations they join. Because every transition deserves more
      than advice: it deserves a strategy.
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Content Widget **************** About us ****** -->

  <Content
    id="about"
    isReversed
    tagline="About us"
    title="Who we are"
    image={{
      src: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1521737711867-e3b97375f902?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=1740&q=80',
      alt: 'Mia Consultancy team working together',
    }}
  >
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <p class="mb-4">
        We came to this from different backgrounds: psychology, sport, statistics, teaching, and a good deal of
        ordinary life. What we had in common was the experience of watching good systems fail people quietly, and of
        being inside those systems while it happened. So we did what our training tells us to do with something that
        keeps repeating: we treated it as a problem worth studying rather than a run of bad luck.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        A boy who joins an academy at ten and is told at nineteen that he is finished. A graduate who leaves a job
        within the first year and cannot quite say why. And the other side of the same story, a club that loses a
        player it spent a decade developing, or a manager who concludes that this generation simply does not want to
        work. Different worlds, same shape: a system that is excellent at its technical task and unpractised at the
        human one, and a handful of transition points that belong to nobody's job description.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        That is the layer we work on. We are academics, psychologists, therapists and statisticians, which means we
        argue with each other productively and we do not take a claim seriously until someone has tried to measure
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are also clear about what we are not: we are not coaches, we are not an HR department, and we do not
        provide therapy inside the organisations we advise. When someone needs that support, our role is to design
        and build the route to it.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Content Widget **************** Where we are ****** -->

  <Content
    isAfterContent
    tagline="Where we work"
    title="Where we are"
    image={{
      src: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517048676732-d65bc937f952?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=1740&q=80',
      alt: 'Team mapping out a plan on a whiteboard',
    }}
  >
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <p class="mb-4">
        People move through life-changing transitions every day. A young athlete enters an elite academy. A graduate
        takes their first step into professional life. An organisation welcomes a new generation of employees with
        different expectations, values, and ways of working.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Most systems are built to achieve technical excellence, yet few are designed for the human experience of
        change. People are recruited, trained, promoted, and evaluated, but the moments where confidence, identity,
        motivation, and belonging are shaped are often left to chance.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">That is where we work.</p>
      <p>
        We design evidence-based psychological and organisational solutions that help individuals thrive and
        organisations build environments where people can grow, perform, and belong. Every programme is tailored to
        the unique needs of the people and institutions we work with.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Features Widget *************** Core Competencies ****** -->

  <Features
    tagline="Core Competencies"
    title="Where we make the difference"
    columns={2}
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Elite Sport',
        description:
          'Supporting athletes, academies, coaches, and families through the psychological demands of development, performance, injury, and the transition to professional sport.',
        icon: 'tabler:ball-football',
      },
      {
        title: 'Organisations',
        description:
          'Helping organisations attract, integrate, and retain the next generation of professionals through evidence-based onboarding, leadership development, wellbeing, and organisational culture.',
        icon: 'tabler:building',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- CallToAction Widget *********** -->

  <CallToAction
    actions={[
      {
        variant: 'primary',
        text: 'Explore our core competencies',
        href: getPermalink('/expertise'),
      },
    ]}
    title="Every transition deserves more than advice."
    subtitle="It deserves a strategy. See how we work with athletes and organisations."
  />
</Layout>
